Add at top of ItemDatabase:

```gdscript
# 选人界面「出装调整」写入：英雄名 → 自定义顺序的推荐出装 id 数组
var recommended_overrides: Dictionary = {}

## 取该英雄在选人界面确认过的出装顺序（无则返回空数组）
func get_recommended_override(hero_name: String) -> Array:
	return recommended_overrides.get(hero_name, [])

func set_recommended_override(hero_name: String, ids: Array) -> void:
	if ids.is_empty():
		recommended_overrides.erase(hero_name)
	else:
		recommended_overrides[hero_name] = ids.duplicate()
```
Also a deterministic default list for select UI: add `func get_default_build(hero_name: String, role: String) -> Array` returning hero's first build if available else role pool. But builds dict is local to function. Move `builds` out? Minimal: add helper that returns first element:
```gdscript
func get_default_build(hero_name: String, role: String) -> Array:
	# 选人界面默认推荐：英雄专属方案 1（无专属则按职责通用方案）
	var all := _recommended_builds(hero_name)
	if not all.is_empty(): return (all[0] as Array).duplicate()
	return get_recommended_items(role).duplicate()
```
But `builds` is local; refactor: extract local dict to `const`? Simplest: change `get_recommended_items` to use a shared member `_builds` initialized lazily... That's a bigger refactor of a 150-line dict. Alternative: in select UI, use `ItemDatabase.get_recommended_items(role)` (role pool) as the default list — deterministic and matches what battle would use without override. Consistency: battle uses role pool → same list ✓. Good: module edits role-pool list. Hero-specific builds ignored (they're random anyway). So no ItemDatabase refactor needed beyond overrides + UI_Manager hook.

Define:
```gdscript
var recommended_overrides: Dictionary = {}

func set_recommended_override(hero_name: String, ids: Array) -> void:
	if ids.is_empty(): recommended_overrides.erase(hero_name)
	else: recommended_overrides[hero_name] = ids.duplicate()

func get_recommended_override(hero_name: String) -> Array:
	return recommended_overrides.get(hero_name, [])
```

UI_Manager `_get_recommended_items`:
```gdscript
func _get_recommended_items(hero) -> Array:
	if cached_recommended_for != hero.display_name:
		var ov: Array = ItemDatabase.get_recommended_override(hero.display_name)
		if not ov.is_empty():
			cached_recommended_list = ov.duplicate()
		else:
			cached_recommended_list = ItemDatabase.get_recommended_items(hero.role)
		cached_recommended_for = hero.display_name
	return cached_recommended_list
```
Cache keyed by display_name but override may be set after select → before battle so fine; but if UI_Manager cached before battle? cache only populated after hero exists. OK.

Implement now.

